  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="work" n="92">
        <pb n="132"/>
        <head>92 — i — II. — <quote>Sing to the Lord a new song</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="preface">
          <ab n="1">Again Hymns on Persons Baptized.</ab>
        </div>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="2">Ye that by enlightening <pb n="133"/> baptism have been made new, by deeds themselves keep [such a<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> reputation unto the end. Do not wantonly betake yourselves back again to the old age of sins; do not in any wise follow after deeds of darkness. You have rightly confessed one<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/> Lord and one faith : [renounce the many doctrines<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/> of error that are falsified against the truth. Lo! you have been armed with the mighty arms of the Spirit : fight and struggle; and do not through [sin that you serve<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/> make miserable treaties with your foes. By calling the<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/> holy Father in heaven <quote>our Father</quote> fix the hidden eyes of your mind constantly on heaven. You have been hallowed by the divine laver; you have been removed from all filth and pollution and stain. Having once been buried and risen together<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a7" target="#n7" n="7"/> with <persName>Christ</persName> who is God, who once suffered and rose, think not at all of a second baptism. Keep the treasure of immortality that has <pb n="134"/> been bestowed upon you with all carefulness, [offering praise to the good Giver of<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a8" target="#n8" n="8"/> this according to the riches of his great mercy.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 132, n. 4</orig></choice> Ps. xcviii, 1.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 133, n. 1</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>the</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 133, n. 2</orig></choice> Eph. iv, 3-6.</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 133, n. 3</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>reject the many opinions (representing <foreign xml:lang="grc">δόξας</foreign>)</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 133, n. 4</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>the fact of sinning</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 133, n. 5</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>upon the</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 133, n. 6</orig></choice> Col. ii, 11-13 (verbal diff.).</note>
        <note xml:id="n8" target="#a8" n="8"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 134, n. 1</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>singing praise to him who gives</quote>.</note>
      </noteGrp>
